# Framework 2: Bilateral Relations / International Organisations Framework

### Hierarchy
[Hierarchy 1] [Subject: INTERNATIONAL RELATIONS] [Section Group: Global Geopolitics & Indian Diaspora] [Microtopic: Groupings & Agreements: Bilateral, Regional & Global Groupings & Agreements Involving or Affecting India's Interests] [Subtopic: Bilateral Relations]
[Hierarchy 2] [Subject: INTERNATIONAL RELATIONS] [Section Group: Global Geopolitics & Indian Diaspora] [Microtopic: Groupings & Agreements: Bilateral, Regional & Global Groupings & Agreements Involving or Affecting India's Interests] [Subtopic: Groupings beyond South Asia]
[Hierarchy 3] [Subject: INTERNATIONAL RELATIONS] [Section Group: Global Geopolitics & Indian Diaspora] [Microtopic: Groupings & Agreements: Bilateral, Regional & Global Groupings & Agreements Involving or Affecting India's Interests] [Subtopic: Groupings involving Immediate and Extended neighbours]
[Hierarchy 4] [Subject: INTERNATIONAL RELATIONS] [Section Group: International Organizations] [Microtopic: International Institutions: Structure, Mandate & Functioning of Important Agencies & Fora] [Subtopic: United Nations and its Agencies]

## Bilateral Relations / International Organisations Framework

### Diagram: Bilateral Relations / International Organisations Framework
![Bilateral Relations / International Organisations Framework](https://pub-cfb8b9095d7d4914990dbb6f73afeb92.r2.dev/general/frameworks/images/bilateral_relations_framework.png)

### Framework Breakdown
- **Intro**: Most recent summit / conference / formation, background
- **Body**:
  - **Dimensions covered by organisation (Dimensions TEST - GICE)**:
    - **Trade and Commerce**: Economic ties, trade volume, agreements
    - **Technology**: Digital cooperation, R&D, space, cybersecurity
    - **Energy**: Renewable energy, oil/gas, nuclear energy cooperation
    - **Security**: Defence ties, joint exercises, counter-terrorism
    - **Environment / Climate change**: Green initiatives, climate commitments
    - **Culture**: People-to-people ties, tourism, diaspora
    - **Geo-strategic & Infrastructure**: Connectivity projects, maritime security, strategic alignments
  - **India's role**:
    - **Achievements / Contributions**: Key leadership roles, initiatives driven by India
    - **Challenges / Constraints**: Friction points, structural bottlenecks
    - **Way forward / Expectations**: Future roadmaps, strategic opportunities
- **Conclusion**: Achievements → Challenges → Way forward / Reforms → Future relevance

